<Base title="Features" description="A connected Cloudflare product foundation with optional, receipt-backed modules."><PageIntro title="A product foundation, not a code dump." description="The Starter keeps infrastructure, identity, product operations, documentation, and releases connected while optional capabilities remain removable." /><section class="content-section"><h2>Core capabilities</h2><div class="fact-list"><div><dt>Project assembly</dt><dd>Local configuration writes a reviewed Blueprint. AI plans and applies only the selected packs.</dd></div><div><dt>Identity</dt><dd>Better Auth owns sign-in, verification, sessions, preferences, and platform Admin authority.</dd></div><div><dt>Operations</dt><dd>A small support inbox and audit trail cover early product needs without importing a helpdesk platform.</dd></div><div><dt>Documentation</dt><dd>Public Starlight docs and the internal Development Plan share repository-owned sources.</dd></div><div><dt>Release</dt><dd>Development and Production use distinct Workers, domains, secrets, databases, evidence, and rollback state.</dd></div></div></section><section class="content-section"><h2>Capabilities arrive through owned seams.</h2><p>Maps, billing, organizations, growth pages, and future modules can add code, dependencies, routes, and SQL without becoming permanent baggage in every copied project.</p></section><CallToAction title="Choose the smallest useful assembly." body="Start with identity and operations, then add capabilities only when the product brief requires them." /></Base>
